    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0359" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg317"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 434.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 19, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your attention will doubtless have been
                    drawn to the report of a debate in the House of Lords, on Monday evening, the
                    15th instant, on the questions raised by the Earl of Clanricarde respecting the
                    action of the United States vessels on the ocean. It will be some cause of
                    satisfaction to you to find both Lord Russell and the Duke of Somerset ready to
                    bear testimony to the fairness of the proceedings of the commanders, and
                    particularly to the deportment of Admiral Wilkes. Considering the predisposition
                    that unquestionably prevails here to find fault with everything done on the part
                    of the United States, it is rather a causes of congratulation to find that the
                    steady policy of the government is gradually compelling testimony to its comity,
                    in the execution of its conceded rights.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
